## Releasing

Push a tag: `git tag v0.1.0 && git push origin v0.1.0`. `.github/workflows/release.yml`
builds the app, packs it with [Velopack](https://velopack.io) and publishes
`{{ desktop_name }}-win-Setup.exe` as the GitHub release for that tag. That release is
the download link to share.
{{#updater}}
Installed copies check the same releases on launch and offer a restart once the newer
version has downloaded.
{{/updater}}

Until the `VPK_SIGN_PARAMS` repository secret holds a code-signing certificate's
signtool arguments, the installer is unsigned and Windows SmartScreen warns on download.
{{/desktop}}

In VS Code, `Ctrl+Shift+B` runs the default build task and the task quick-pick
(`Ctrl+Shift+P` → "Run Task") lists everything else, each with a one-line `detail`
explaining what it costs and what it touches.

